        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is AKLUER a legit brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. AKLUER has its own store at akluer.com, a written one-year warranty, a return policy, US support by email and phone, and spare parts for its pads, and Amazon lists it as the manufacturer of its listings. It does not publish a company name or address, and most Amazon listings are sold by third-party sellers, so check who the seller is.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are AKLUER walking pads any good?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For slow walking at a desk, they are reasonable budget pads. The basic 480L-A is light, quiet by its listing and cheap. They are not built for running, the 2.5 HP motor figure is a peak rating, and the warranty is one year, so expect budget-pad durability.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does AKLUER give?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One year on the frame, motor and parts, for the original purchaser, according to AKLUER’s warranty page in November 2026. You must activate it by submitting your order details on AKLUER’s site or scanning the QR code on the treadmill. Parts sent after the first 15 days carry shipping fees.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How fast does an AKLUER walking pad go?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The basic 480L-A, Z1 and 480L-B go 0.6 to 4.0 mph. The TW140X and P3-D go to 6.2 mph. The H1-B’s current Amazon listing says 7.6 mph, but an earlier independent spec sheet recorded 4 mph, so confirm with the seller.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the weight limit on AKLUER treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Every AKLUER on Amazon in November 2026 was listed at 330 lb, including the manual RJ-401. If you are near that figure, choose a pad rated higher and keep sessions moderate, because a light pad running at its limit wears faster.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why are there so many AKLUER listings for the same pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Several sellers list the 480L-A under different titles, colours and prices; on 21 November 2026 we found it from $69.99 to $118.99. Check the model number in the product details, the seller and the stock before choosing the cheapest.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can I return an AKLUER bought on Amazon to AKLUER?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              AKLUER’s refund policy says it only accepts returns for orders placed on its own site, with a 15-day window and a 15% fee on change-of-mind refunds. An Amazon order follows Amazon’s returns, or the third-party seller’s, so check the seller before you buy.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

